      "problem": "Factor $8n^3 + m^6.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\na^3+b^3=(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n8n^3 + m^6 = (2n)^3 + (m^2)^3\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{n}^{3}+{m}^{6} & =(2n)^{3}+({m}^{2})^{3} \\\\  & =(2n+{m}^{2})((2n)^{2}-2n\\cdot {m}^{2}+({m}^{2})^{2}) \\\\  & =(2n+{m}^{2})(4{n}^{2}-2{m}^{2}n+{m}^{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
